p-value that says so.

The model is fitted by \code{\link[caret:train]{caret::train()}} with \code{method = "lm"}, so the fit itself
is \code{\link[stats:lm]{stats::lm()}}'s and the resampling is \code{caret}'s. Two consequences are worth
knowing:

\describe{
\item{Cross-validation does not change the model}{\code{cv} decides whether the
model is scored, not how it is fitted. The final model is fitted on all
usable rows either way, so the coefficients of \code{cv = TRUE} and
\code{cv = FALSE} are identical and only \code{performance} and \code{resampling}
